[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[Variation "Alapin Variation"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "d4-pawn-centre,bishop-trade,space-advantage"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4...Bb4+"]
[Start "e6-main-line 4.cxd4"]

4... Bb4+ ( 4... Nc6 { Joins the line 2...Nc6 3.d4 cxd4 4.cxd4 e6, where White pushes 5.d5. } ) ( 4... Nf6 5. e5 { Kicks the knight. After 5...Nd5 6.Nf3 the game joins the line 2...Nf6 3.e5 Nd5 4.d4 cxd4 5.Nf3 e6 6.cxd4. } 5... Nd5 6. Nf3 ) ( 4... a6 5. Nf3 d5 ( 5... Nf6 6. Bd3 ) 6. e5 ) ( 4... d6 { Joins the line 2...d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.cxd4 e6, where 5.Nc3 guards e4. } ) 5. Bd2 { Offers to trade bishops. Black's dark-squared bishop is its best minor piece in this structure, while White's on c1 has little to do. } 5... Bxd2+ 6. Qxd2 d5 7. e5 { Gains space and keeps Black's knight off f6. With the dark-squared bishops gone, Black has no easy way to attack the pawn chain on d4 and e5. } 7... Ne7 8. Nc3 Nbc6 9. Nf3 O-O 10. Bd3 { Plan: castle, keep the pawns on d4 and e5, put a rook on c1 along the open c-file, and look for a kingside attack with the bishop on d3 and the knights. } *
